6.1 Automatic Split-Screen Layout
=================================

When you launch ‘dired-image-thumbnail’ (or use standard ‘image-dired’
with this package loaded):

     +------------------+------------------------+
     |  Thumbnails      |  Full-size Image       |
     |  (Left 40%)      |  (Right 60%)           |
     |                  |                        |
     |  [img1] <--      |  +------------------+  |
     |  [img2]          |  |                  |  |
     |  [img3]          |  |   Current Image  |  |
     |  [img4]          |  |                  |  |
     |  [img5]          |  +------------------+  |
     |                  |                        |
     +------------------+------------------------+

   The layout is controlled by ‘dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout’
(default ‘left-right’) and ‘dired-image-thumbnail-window-ratio’ (default
‘0.4’).


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Auto-Display Navigation,  Next: Quick Deletion Workflow,  Prev: Automatic Split-Screen Layout,  Up: Enhanced Workflow

6.2 Auto-Display Navigation
===========================

With ‘dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate’ enabled (default):

   • Press ‘n’ or ‘p’ to navigate thumbnails
   • The full-size image automatically updates on the right
   • No need to press <RET> or ‘C-<RET>’ for each image
   • Smooth, fluid browsing experience


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Quick Deletion Workflow,  Prev: Auto-Display Navigation,  Up: Enhanced Workflow

6.3 Quick Deletion Workflow
===========================

Press ‘C-d’ in either the thumbnail or image display buffer to:

  1. Get a confirmation prompt (unless
     ‘dired-image-thumbnail-auto-accept’ is enabled)
  2. Delete the current image file
  3. Automatically advance to the next image
  4. Continue browsing seamlessly

   This makes culling large photo collections much faster than the
standard workflow.


