7.2 In Thumbnail Buffer
=======================

Navigation
----------

‘n’
‘f’
‘<RIGHT>’
     Next image (auto-display when enabled)
‘p’
‘b’
‘<LEFT>’
     Previous image (auto-display when enabled)
‘+’
     Increase thumbnail size
‘-’
     Decrease thumbnail size

   When ‘dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate’ is enabled
(default), pressing ‘n’ or ‘p’ (also ‘f’ or ‘b’) automatically displays
the full-size image.  When follow is activated and the image window
opens, the thumbnails are automatically refreshed so they re-align and
the columns fit the new thumbnail window width.

Sorting
-------

‘s’
‘S’
     Select sort criteria with ‘completing-read’ (dired order, name,
     date, size, reverse)

Filtering
---------

‘/’
‘\’
     Select filter criteria with ‘completing-read’ (name, size, clear)

Display
-------

‘g’
     Refresh the display
‘G’
     Clear cache and refresh (hard refresh)
‘+’
     Increase thumbnail size
‘-’
     Decrease thumbnail size
‘Q’
     Select display quality with ‘completing-read’ (full, high, fast,
     faster, draft)

Marking
-------

‘m’
     Mark image and, with follow on, advance to the next image through
     the fast preview pipeline
‘u’
     Unmark image (same follow behaviour)
‘M’
     Mark all images
‘U’
     Unmark all
‘t’
     Toggle all marks

File Operations
---------------

‘D’
     Delete image at point
‘C-d’
     Delete image and move to next
‘x’
     Delete all marked images
‘d’
     Jump to file in Dired

Other
-----

‘W’
     Open in external editor
‘?’
     Open the transient menu (all commands)


