9.3 Window Layout
=================

Control the split-screen layout and thumbnail/image ratio:

     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-window-layout 'left-right) ; 'left-right, 'right-left, 'top-bottom, 'bottom-top, 'thumb-only, or nil
     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-window-ratio 0.4)          ; Fraction of frame for thumbnails

   Set to ‘nil’ to disable automatic layout management and use your own
‘display-buffer-alist’ rules.


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Display Quality,  Next: Image Validation,  Prev: Window Layout,  Up: Customization

9.4 Display Quality
===================

Control the speed/fidelity trade-off when navigating with ‘n’/‘p’:

     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-display-quality 'faster) ; 'full, 'high, 'fast, 'faster, or 'draft

   Lower quality levels use external tools (‘djpeg’/‘cjpeg’ for JPEGs,
‘magick’ for others) to generate small preview files, so Emacs decodes
less data.  Press ‘Q’ in the thumbnail buffer to cycle through levels
interactively.


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Image Validation,  Next: External Editor,  Prev: Display Quality,  Up: Customization

9.5 Image Validation
====================

Control which files are accepted as images:

     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-minimum-file-size 100) ; Minimum bytes (0 to disable)
     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-validate-headers t)    ; Check magic bytes

   When ‘dired-image-thumbnail-validate-headers’ is non-nil, each
candidate file is opened briefly to verify that its first few bytes
match a known image format signature (JPEG, PNG, GIF, BMP, TIFF, WEBP,
ICO, HEIC/HEIF). SVG files are accepted without a byte check since they
are XML text.


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: External Editor,  Next: Navigation Behavior,  Prev: Image Validation,  Up: Customization

9.6 External Editor
===================

Set a specific program for ‘W’ to open images with:

     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-external-editor "gimp") ; nil for system default

   When ‘nil’ (default), the system default application is used via
‘xdg-open’ on Linux, ‘open’ on macOS, or ‘start’ on Windows.


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Navigation Behavior,  Next: Auto-Accepting Actions,  Prev: External Editor,  Up: Customization

9.7 Navigation Behavior
=======================

Control whether navigating with ‘n’/‘p’ automatically displays full-size
images:

     (setq dired-image-thumbnail-auto-display-on-navigate t) ; Auto-display on n/p

   When enabled (default), pressing ‘n’ or ‘p’ in the thumbnail buffer
automatically updates the image display buffer.  When disabled, you must
press <RET> or ‘C-<RET>’ to view full-size images.


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Auto-Accepting Actions,  Next: Image Extensions,  Prev: Navigation Behavior,  Up: Customization

