11.1 Reviewing a Photo Collection
=================================

  1. Open directory in Dired: ‘C-x d ~/Photos <RET>’
  2. Insert subdirectories with images: ‘C-t s’
  3. View thumbnails: ‘C-t m’
  4. Thumbnails appear on the left, full-size view on the right
  5. Sort by date (newest first): ‘s’, choose ‘date’, then ‘s’, choose
     ‘reverse’
  6. Browse with ‘n’ / ‘p’ -- images automatically update on the right
  7. Mark keepers with ‘m’, jump to Dired with ‘d’


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Finding Large Images,  Next: Quick Culling Workflow,  Prev: Reviewing a Photo Collection,  Up: Workflow Examples

11.2 Finding Large Images
=========================

  1. View thumbnails: ‘C-t m’
  2. Grid appears on left, image display on right
  3. Filter by size: ‘/’ and choose ‘size’, then enter ‘1M’ for minimum,
     leave maximum empty
  4. Sort by size (largest first): ‘s’, choose ‘size’, then ‘s’, choose
     ‘reverse’
  5. Navigate with ‘n’/‘p’ to review each image
  6. Mark images for deletion with ‘m’, delete with ‘x’
  7. Or use ‘C-d’ to delete current image and advance to next


File: dired-image-thumbnail.info,  Node: Quick Culling Workflow,  Next: Finding High-Resolution Images,  Prev: Finding Large Images,  Up: Workflow Examples

